SUMMARY:'Music Under the June Moon’ Concert in Anderson Park
DESCRIPTION:The moon\, the crickets and free chamber music in Anderson Park: Bring a picnic and a blanket and enjoy the Chamber Music Society of North Jersey perform al fresco in historic Anderson Park. Friends of Anderson Park is celebrating its tenth “Music Under the June Moon” concert by presenting Felix Mendelssohn’s ambitious String Octet and the String Quartet by Fanny Mendelssohn (Hensel)\, as well as other works. The full concert program will be posted at FriendsOfAndersonPark.com. At Essex County Anderson Park\, 274 Bellevue Avenue\, Montclair. Rain date is June 7\, same time. (Check the Friends of Anderson Park Facebook page for weather updates or call 973-477-7207.) \nSponsored by Friends of Anderson Park and the Essex County Department of Parks\, Recreation and Cultural Affairs. Made possible by funds from the Essex County Division of Cultural Affairs\, a partner of the New Jersey State Council on the Arts; and a generous donation from the Bravitas Group/Silver Family Foundation. Handicap parking information is at FriendsOfAndersonPark.com. \nShare this:\n				Share on Facebook (Opens in new window)\n				Facebook\n			\n				Share on Bluesky (Opens in new window)\n				Bluesky\n			\n				Share on LinkedIn (Opens in new window)\n				LinkedIn\n			\n				Share on Threads (Opens in new window)\n				Threads\n			\n				Share on Nextdoor (Opens in new window)\n				Nextdoor\n			\n				Share on WhatsApp (Opens in new window)\n				WhatsApp\n			\n				Email a link to a friend (Opens in new window)\n				Email
